'''Quermians''' were a gaunt, long-necked [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Quermia]]. They had two [[brain]]s, one located inside their head and the other within their chest cavity, and two pairs of [[Limb|arms]]. During the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[Invasion of Naboo]], four Quermians were enrolled in the [[Jedi Order]], one of whom was [[Jedi Master]] [[Yarael Poof]], a member of the [[Jedi High Council]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:YaraelPoof_HRCE.png|thumb|left|150px|Yarael Poof's two sets of arms]]
Quermians were a willowy<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> [[humanoid]]<ref name="Card Trader" /> garden<ref name="VE" /> [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that had pasty [[Color|white]] skin and red [[eye]]s, which were located in a bulbous head with a small [[mouth]] that was located on top of a craning neck.<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> They had two [[brain]]s,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> one located in their head and the other inside their chest cavity.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> Possessing no spines,<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> Quermians were notable for their towering stature,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> with an average member of the species standing over three [[Foot|feet]] taller than most other humanoids.<ref name="Card Trader" /> Quermians had two sets of thin [[Limb|arms]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> with hands that terminated in several slender digits, and a pair of legs that ended in large toed feet.<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> The second pair of arms was often hidden and was supported by the brain located in the chest cavity.<ref name="VE" /> Lacking [[nose]]s, Quermians instead smelled using olfactory glands in their hands.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> Quermians could live up to 200 years of age, possibly more. Due to the Quermian's many physical and genetic similarities to the [[Xexto]], [[xenobiologist]]s believed them to share a common ancestor.<ref name="Helmet Colletion 76">{{HelmetCollectionCite|76|Databank A-Z}}</ref> In reality, Quermians were created from the Xexto species by the ancient [[Arkanian]] [[scientist]]s.<ref name="SS">''[[Savage Spirits]]''</ref>

==Society and culture==
Some Quermians, such as [[Jedi Master]] [[Yarael Poof]], preferred to conceal their second set of arms beneath clothing,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and traditionally wore [[cannom collar]]s.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> Poof claimed his surname was a grand and historic name among his people.<ref name="LivingForce">''[[The Living Force]]''</ref> An entry on Quermians was included in "[[Species From A to Z]]," a survival compendium sent out by [[Carson Teva]] during the [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="OSWM">{{GermanFanCite|114|Database}}</ref>

==Quermians in the galaxy==
[[Homeworld|Native]] to<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> [[Planet|world]] of [[Quermia]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> four Quermians were members of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[Invasion of Naboo]], the most senior of which being Jedi Master Yarael Poof. A revered member of the [[Jedi High Council|Jedi Council]], he was a celebrated [[diplomat]] and [[teacher]],<ref name="Card Trader" /> and an expert practitioner of [[Jedi]] [[mind trick]]s and illusions.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" />

[[Senator]] [[Nim Tar]] of the [[New Republic]] was a Quermian.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Quermians first appeared in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> Although never identified on screen, the species was first identified in [[Star Wars: Episode I: The Visual Dictionary|''Star Wars: Episode I The Visual Dictionary'']], a 1999 [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] reference book written by [[David West Reynolds (real person)|David West Reynolds]].<ref name="The Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Episode I: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> The species' name was confirmed to be [[canon]] by [[Star Wars: Card Trader|''Star Wars'': Card Trader]], an app released on [[Wikipedia:iOS|iOS]] and [[Wikipedia:Android (operating system)|Android]] platforms by [[Topps|The Topps Company, Inc.]] in [[2015]].<ref name="Card Trader" />

Despite being a member of the [[Xexto]] species,<ref name="Ezra's Gamble">''[[Ezra's Gamble]]''</ref> [[Ferpil Wallaway]] bears a striking resemblance to a Quermian,<ref name="Rebel Journal">''[[Rebel Journal by Ezra Bridger]]''</ref> who were a species of genetically modified Xexto.<ref name="SS">''[[Savage Spirits]]''</ref>

